course: dictionary
lesson: 12321
title: Corrupted: broken, dishonest or changed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Corrupted» is the past form of the verb «corrupt». It can mean three things: broken, dishonest, or changed from how it should be. Context tells you which meaning fits.
explain: «The photo would not open because the file was corrupted.» Here a corrupted file is damaged, so it will not open or works wrongly. That is why people keep backup copies of important files.
explain: «The guard was corrupted by the bribe he was offered and let the thief go.» Here corrupted means made dishonest. The clues are bribe and let the thief go, which show that his good character had been changed for the worse.
fact: «Corrupted» is the past form of the verb «corrupt».
fact: A «corrupted» file or piece of data has been damaged, so it cannot open or works wrongly.
fact: «Corrupted» can also mean made dishonest or morally bad, especially by money or power.
fact: A «corrupted» word or text has been changed from its original form, often by mistake.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The file would not open because it was corrupted.» What does corrupted mean here? | Printed in full colour | Made into a shiny new copy | Locked with a password | *Damaged, so it cannot open or works wrongly
exercise: «The guard was corrupted by the money he was offered.» What does corrupted suggest? | Made calm and cheerful | Made into a bird | Made taller and stronger | *Made dishonest
exercise: Find the past form of the verb corrupt. | corrupts | corrupt | corrupting | *corrupted
test:
Ella says, «My homework is corrupted, the screen only shows dots.» What does she probably mean? | *The file is damaged and will not open properly | Her homework is finished and perfect | Her homework is written in a secret code | Her homework is printed in bright colours
test:
«The old map showed a corrupted version of the town's name.» What does corrupted mean here? | Painted in bright colours | Made longer and fancier | *Changed from its original form, often by mistake | Shown on a big screen
exam:
Why is it a good idea to keep a backup copy of a file in case it becomes corrupted? | Backups make the file load faster | *So you still have a working copy if the first one is damaged | Backups stop the computer from getting hot | A backup is only needed for photos
